<!--
  RESEARCH CONSENT GATE

  The deployed route "/" lands here, not on the course. Three states:
  * unanswered → the IRB form
  * answered but not acknowledged → a short acknowledgment
  * acknowledged → the course itself

  Gates test ANSWERED (any value); declining changes nothing about the course

  The form block is also a child of the main course (same block),
  giving students the opportunity to opt-out or opt-in later.

  Version of the consent form can be had from event logs, which should
  tie back to a specific release key. We may consider adding an event
  explicitly including form version in the future.
-->

<Vertical id="wj_study" title="Writing Journals (Research Study)" launchable="true">

<!-- HACK: when= directly on these <Use> tags rendered unconditionally,
     so the gating lives on wrapper Verticals. <Use> supports
     attribute overrides and when= is supposed to work — platform bug;
     unwrap when fix is confirmed. -->

<Vertical id="wj_irb_form_gate" when="!@wj_irb_consent.value">
<Use ref="wj_irb_consent_form" />
</Vertical>

<Vertical id="wj_irb_ack" when="@wj_irb_consent.value && !@wj_irb_ack_done.value">
<Markdown when="@wj_irb_consent.value === 'consented'">
## Thank you

Your course work may be included in the research, always de-identified. You
can change your answer at any time under **Research Consent** in the course
navigation.
</Markdown>
<Markdown when="@wj_irb_consent.value === 'declined'">
## No problem

Your course work stays out of the research. Nothing about the course changes —
same activities, same credit. You can change your answer at any time under
**Research Consent** in the course navigation.
</Markdown>
<ActionButton id="wj_irb_ack_btn" label="Continue to the Writing Journals">
<SetFieldAction id="wj_irb_ack_set" target="wj_irb_ack_done" field="value" value="acknowledged" />
</ActionButton>
</Vertical>

<Vertical id="wj_course_gate" when="@wj_irb_consent.value && @wj_irb_ack_done.value">
<Use ref="wj_course" />
</Vertical>

<!-- The form definition, parked unrendered (the <Use> above and the course
     nav render it). Same pattern as wj1's card deck. -->
<Hidden id="wj_consent_defs">
<!-- Flag holder for the acknowledgment. SetFieldAction needs a real block to
     write into, so the flag is parked here unrendered — same pattern as wj1's
     wj1_type_choice. It is a LineInput, not a Done: SetFieldAction validates
     the value against the TARGET FIELD'S SCHEMA, and Done's value is boolean
     (z_olx_boolean), so writing the semantic code "acknowledged" threw inside
     the action and the button did nothing at all. LineInput's value is a
     plain string, so the stored value can say what happened. -->
<LineInput id="wj_irb_ack_done" />

<Vertical id="wj_irb_consent_form" title="Research Consent">

<TalkBubble who="Katie Fredlund" cast="consent.cast">
<Markdown>
As the Director of First-Year Writing, I am always working to improve
how writing is taught at the University of Memphis and to identify the
learning activities that most effectively support and engage our
students. To do this, I conduct research about how students learn to
think and write. In order to learn what our students need, I look at
how students complete writing and thinking activities. I collect this
information to improve our courses and the instruction in the program
overall. As an added benefit, I often learn new ways to support
writing instructors beyond the UofM. Sometimes, I want to share what I
have learned, and I can only do that if you are okay with me using
your responses to the Writing Process Journals in my research.
</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>

<Markdown>
# University of Memphis

## Informed Consent

**Title:** Scenario-Based Assessment in the age of generative AI: Making space in the education market for alternative assessment paradigms

**Principal Investigator:** Dr. John Sabatini

**Sponsor:** Institute for Intelligent Systems (IIS)

## Procedures

You are being asked to take part in a research study. If you decide to
take part, you will agree to share some of your course work with the
researchers. This work includes writing assignments, online
discussions, and assessments you produce for the course. These
materials will be obtained after grades are submitted and
will be accessed only by the researchers.

No work beyond that which you would normally do as part of this course
will be required. The research will require no more time than you
would normally spend on the course. The decision to participate, or
not to take part, will have no effect on your grade or standing in
this class.

Your instructor will not know whether you consented to this research
until after they submit the grades for the course. You will not
interact with any of the other researchers.

## Voluntary Participation and Withdrawal

You do not have to be in this study, and you may choose to leave the study at any time.

## Contact Information

Contact Professor Katherine Fredlund at kfrdlund@memphis.edu.

## Consent

Please choose one. Either answer takes you into the course.
</Markdown>

<ChoiceInput id="wj_irb_consent">
  <Key value="consented"> I accept. </Key>
  <Key value="declined" > I do not want to participate in this study. </Key>
</ChoiceInput>

</Vertical> <!-- wj_irb_consent_form -->
</Hidden>
</Vertical> <!-- wj_study -->
